    <string name="ssh_auth_server">Server: %1$s</string>
    <string name="ssh_hint_tailscale_server">• Port 22 is served by Tailscale SSH, which ignores keys and passwords and only checks your tailnet policy. Allow this device to log in as %1$s in the policy\'s \"ssh\" rules, or turn off Tailscale SSH on the node (tailscale set --ssh=false) to use OpenSSH.</string>
    <string name="ssh_hint_works_elsewhere">• If this key works from another computer, run ssh -v %1$s@%2$s there: the \"Authenticated … using\" and \"Server accepts key\" lines show which key, user and address it really uses</string>
    <string name="ssh_hint_dropbear_keys">• Dropbear (OpenWrt) reads root\'s keys from /etc/dropbear/authorized_keys</string>
    <string name="ssh_hint_from_restriction">• A from=\"…\" option on the key line, or Match Address / AllowUsers in sshd_config, rejects connections from tailnet addresses (100.x)</string>
    <string name="ssh_hint_server_log">• The node\'s log states the exact reason: journalctl -u ssh -n 20</string>
